Ticket work (functional or purely technical) goes through **PILOT**, a lightweight
alternative to running the full BMAD-METHOD agent framework — five short phases
(`plan` → `investigate` → `lay out` → `operate` → `test & validate`), each its own
isolated, low-token agent context instead of one accumulating one. It's provided by the
`pilot` Claude Code plugin (github.com/Jonas-Eve/pilot, pinned in
`.claude/settings.json`) rather than living in this repo: the phase skills are invoked
as `/pilot:story`, `/pilot:scope`, `/pilot:spec`, `/pilot:dev`, `/pilot:review` — driven
one phase at a time, there's no single command that runs the whole pipeline end to
end — and their personas live in the plugin's `agents/pilot-*.md`. `docs/pilot-process.md`
in this repo is a verbatim copy of the plugin's canonical spec — the state machine,
labels, and claim protocol — kept in sync by `/pilot:update`, never hand-edited here.
Read it before creating or moving a ticket through any phase.
